content.p:
 The collection agency shall submit the annual report, the comprehensive audit report (Article 728b paragraph 1 CO

 SR 220
	) and the accounts for the fee to OFCOM by the end of April of the following year at the latest.

The collection agency shall publish the annual invoice (Art. 958 para. 2 CO

 SR 220
	), the audit report (Art. 728b para. 2 CO) and the activity report with the details in terms of Article 64 paragraph 1 by the end of April of the following year at the latest

item.p:
the data under Article 6 letters a-h, j, o-s and u of the Register Harmonisation Act of 23 June 2006

 SR 431.02
	 (RHA);

content.p:
 In the last 12 months before the date of change in system, the previous fee collection agency shall invoice the fee for the remaining time in accordance with the previous staggered scale (Article 60a paragraph 2

 AS 2010 5219
	).

blockList.listIntroduction:
 The previous fee collection agency shall provide the new collection agency at the latest 18 months after this provision comes into force with the following data on persons exempt from the fee (former Art. 64

 AS 2007 787 6657
	), provided the data is available:
